1
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:03,975
Last time, in 2010,

2
00:00:03,995 --> 00:00:05,690
Jupiter became a second sun,

3
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,495
and a message went out to Earth:

4
00:00:07,515 --> 00:00:09,085
all these worlds are yours,

5
00:00:09,105 --> 00:00:10,585
except Europa.

6
00:00:10,605 --> 00:00:13,485
Dave and HAL vanished into the monolith.

7
00:00:13,505 --> 00:00:14,655
There are no more movies,

8
00:00:14,675 --> 00:00:16,005
but Arthur C.

9
00:00:16,025 --> 00:00:17,730
Clarke wrote two more books:

10
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:20,480
2061 and 3001.

11
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:22,480
Clarke said each book is a variation

12
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,205
on a theme,

13
00:00:23,225 --> 00:00:25,030
so details shift a little.

14
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,480
Here's part three.

15
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:27,775
Spoilers ahead!

16
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,225
It's 2061 .

17
00:00:30,245 --> 00:00:32,200
Heywood Floyd is now a hundred and

18
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:33,275
three years old,

19
00:00:33,295 --> 00:00:36,050
kept healthy by living in low gravity.

20
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,825
People call Jupiter's new sun Lucifer,

21
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:42,025
and Europa is hidden under thick clouds.

22
00:00:42,045 --> 00:00:43,900
Floyd is a guest on a luxury

23
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,825
spaceship called Universe,

24
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:47,700
headed for Halley's Comet.

25
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,375
He becomes one of the first people

26
00:00:49,395 --> 00:00:51,224
ever to walk on its surface.

27
00:00:51,959 --> 00:00:54,939
Meanwhile, Floyd's grandson Chris is an officer

28
00:00:54,959 --> 00:00:56,014
on another ship,

29
00:00:56,034 --> 00:00:56,903
the Galaxy.

30
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:59,749
A stewardess tries to hijack it and

31
00:00:59,769 --> 00:01:01,794
force it toward Europa.

32
00:01:01,844 --> 00:01:03,509
The plan goes wrong,

33
00:01:03,529 --> 00:01:06,084
and the Galaxy splashes down in Europa's

34
00:01:06,104 --> 00:01:07,334
new ocean.

35
00:01:07,354 --> 00:01:08,934
The crew is stranded,

36
00:01:08,954 --> 00:01:10,659
on the one world humans were warned

37
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:12,229
to stay away from.

38
00:01:12,349 --> 00:01:14,354
And right nearby is a mountain made

39
00:01:14,374 --> 00:01:15,971
of solid diamond.

40
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:18,472
The mountain is a piece of Jupiter's

41
00:01:18,492 --> 00:01:20,707
old core, blasted out when the planet

42
00:01:20,727 --> 00:01:21,807
collapsed.

43
00:01:21,827 --> 00:01:24,132
The Universe changes course and rescues the

44
00:01:24,152 --> 00:01:25,657
stranded crew.

45
00:01:25,677 --> 00:01:26,432
Along the way,

46
00:01:26,452 --> 00:01:28,107
they glimpse the Europans,

47
00:01:28,127 --> 00:01:31,077
strange creatures crawling out of the sea.

48
00:01:31,177 --> 00:01:33,707
And Clarke reveals that Dave and HAL

49
00:01:33,727 --> 00:01:35,832
still live inside the monolith,

50
00:01:35,852 --> 00:01:36,957
watching.

51
00:01:36,977 --> 00:01:38,682
In about a thousand years,

52
00:01:38,702 --> 00:01:40,250
humans will be judged.

53
00:01:41,007 --> 00:01:43,862
Now jump to the year 3001.

54
00:01:43,882 --> 00:01:45,137
Far out at the edge of the

55
00:01:45,157 --> 00:01:47,886
solar system, a space tug finds a

56
00:01:47,906 --> 00:01:50,367
frozen body drifting in the dark.

57
00:01:50,387 --> 00:01:51,742
It's Frank Poole,

58
00:01:51,762 --> 00:01:55,507
the astronaut HAL sent spinning into space,

59
00:01:55,527 --> 00:01:57,357
a thousand years earlier.

60
00:01:57,377 --> 00:02:00,107
Future medicine brings him back to life.

61
00:02:00,127 --> 00:02:01,557
Frank wakes up in a world he

62
00:02:01,577 --> 00:02:03,120
barely recognizes.

63
00:02:03,904 --> 00:02:06,459
Earth now has four giant towers that

64
00:02:06,479 --> 00:02:08,409
rise from the equator all the way

65
00:02:08,429 --> 00:02:09,759
up into space,

66
00:02:09,779 --> 00:02:11,809
joined by a ring around the planet

67
00:02:11,829 --> 00:02:13,409
where people live.

68
00:02:13,429 --> 00:02:14,834
Instead of screens,

69
00:02:14,854 --> 00:02:17,559
people wear BrainCaps that connect their minds

70
00:02:17,579 --> 00:02:19,309
straight to computers.

71
00:02:19,329 --> 00:02:22,229
Humans live on the moons of Jupiter.

72
00:02:22,354 --> 00:02:24,084
And everyone wants to meet the man

73
00:02:24,104 --> 00:02:25,980
from the year 2001.

74
00:02:26,662 --> 00:02:28,092
Frank travels to Europa,

75
00:02:28,112 --> 00:02:30,067
and something reaches out to him:

76
00:02:30,087 --> 00:02:32,217
Dave Bowman and HAL,

77
00:02:32,237 --> 00:02:33,942
now merged into one mind,

78
00:02:33,962 --> 00:02:35,392
called Halman.

79
00:02:35,412 --> 00:02:37,717
Halman has been inside the monolith all

80
00:02:37,737 --> 00:02:40,222
this time, learning how it works.

81
00:02:40,242 --> 00:02:41,797
And he has a warning.

82
00:02:41,817 --> 00:02:44,022
The monolith is not a god.

83
00:02:44,042 --> 00:02:45,172
It's a machine,

84
00:02:45,192 --> 00:02:46,972
and it's been reporting on humans to

85
00:02:46,992 --> 00:02:48,021
its makers.

86
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:51,032
Those makers are so far away that

87
00:02:51,052 --> 00:02:53,752
their answer took centuries to come back.

88
00:02:53,832 --> 00:02:55,312
Now it has arrived,

89
00:02:55,332 --> 00:02:57,087
and it's bad news.

90
00:02:57,107 --> 00:02:59,362
The monolith's new orders are to wipe

91
00:02:59,382 --> 00:03:00,857
out humanity.

92
00:03:00,942 --> 00:03:02,947
The same machine that taught apes to

93
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:05,072
use tools now plans to end the

94
00:03:05,092 --> 00:03:06,222
story.

95
00:03:06,242 --> 00:03:08,447
Humans have very little time to fight

96
00:03:08,467 --> 00:03:09,084
back.

97
00:03:09,841 --> 00:03:11,871
Deep inside a mountain on the Moon

98
00:03:11,891 --> 00:03:14,421
called Pico, there's a sealed vault of

99
00:03:14,441 --> 00:03:17,971
the most dangerous computer viruses ever made.

100
00:03:17,991 --> 00:03:19,906
Frank's team takes some out,

101
00:03:19,926 --> 00:03:22,331
and Halman carries them into the monolith,

102
00:03:22,351 --> 00:03:24,256
like a Trojan horse.

103
00:03:24,276 --> 00:03:25,856
The plan works.

104
00:03:25,876 --> 00:03:28,246
The virus spreads through the monoliths,

105
00:03:28,266 --> 00:03:29,846
and they shut down for good,

106
00:03:29,866 --> 00:03:31,323
before they can strike.

107
00:03:32,062 --> 00:03:34,067
So that's the whole odyssey.

108
00:03:34,087 --> 00:03:36,837
A monolith taught apes to use tools.

109
00:03:36,927 --> 00:03:38,815
Another called humans to Jupiter.

110
00:03:38,835 --> 00:03:42,092
A third turned Jupiter into a sun.

111
00:03:42,202 --> 00:03:43,032
And in the end,

112
00:03:43,052 --> 00:03:45,307
humans used their own tools to stop

113
00:03:45,327 --> 00:03:46,057
them.

114
00:03:46,077 --> 00:03:47,682
Clarke ends with a hint that the

115
00:03:47,702 --> 00:03:49,757
makers may notice someday.

116
00:03:49,777 --> 00:03:52,364
Until then, the future belongs to us.

